                    <birth when="1000-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Morgan 29.7.1798 at Horne Tooke's / 17.10.1799 Morgan at Parry's (King's
                            Bench Prison) with Malkin and Tooke / 29.11.1799 sleep at Morgan's (near
                            Hurley, Berks) / 16.2.1800 at Horne Tooke's (and Malkin) / 25.2.1800
                            Morgan br (fr?) at (Joseph) Johnson's / 17.5.1800 dines at Milton
                            Gallery (and Malkin) / 16.5.1805 miss Morgan at Wake's.</p>
                        <p> The above Morgan
                            entries, The first
                            entry at Tooke's in 1798 might have been William Morgan or his brother
                            George Cadogan Morgan DNB 1754-1798 who died on 17.11.1798. The others
                            were probably William Morgan, and the miss Morgan at Wake's in 1805 may
                            have been his daughter Sarah who married Benjamin Travers in 1809 and
                            died before 1813 </p>
                    </note>
